{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494170-wyld-cults-and-weaver-cults","id":1494170,"title":"Wyld cults and Weaver cults?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-02T19:09:32-07:00","id":1494170,"title":"Wyld cults and Weaver cults?","content":"How would you all do a Wyld cult or a Weaver cult?<br /> <br /> For a Wyld cult, I\u2019d use some crazy Mythos imagery with an almost fairytale feel layered on it. Belonging to the cult for any real length of time drives you insane as the Wyld sinks into your mind.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine of the Chronicles of Darkness is a pretty god idea, in my opinion, for a Weaver cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T20:06:00-07:00","id":1494173,"title":"","content":"A Weaver cult would probably be based around the idea of everyone in the group sharing the same ideas and opinions, conforming to groupthink and harshly punishing non-conformity. This could be anything from a utopian commune or wider social movement, a scientific think tank or other group all adhering to specific theories or models regardless if real world evidence supports it or not, or transhumanists trying to evolve themselves via cybernetic or genetic technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T21:46:54-07:00","id":1494179,"title":"","content":"The Wyld is the kind of being where it doesn't really matter if you worship it or not, the same things still happen. Humans are unlikely to do so in the first place; the books are quite insistent on their lacking a connection it, as if frayed and broken. Still, if a group thinks that they get results from throwing people into a Threshold, they'll probably keep doing it on account of the self same pattern obsession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T10:33:17-07:00","id":1494232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494170-wyld-cults-and-weaver-cults?p=1494173#post1494173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Weaver cult would probably be based around the idea of everyone in the group sharing the same ideas and opinions, conforming to groupthink and harshly punishing non-conformity. This could be anything from a utopian commune or wider social movement, a scientific think tank or other group all adhering to specific theories or models regardless if real world evidence supports it or not, or transhumanists trying to evolve themselves via cybernetic or genetic technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the transhumanism idea. <br /> <br /> \u201cWhen the difference between tool-user and tool ceases to matter, are you even human anymore? Does it matter? You\u2019re part of the system now, glorious in its inevitability.\u201d<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u201dPraise the Omnissiah!\u201d</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T12:37:36-07:00","id":1494251,"title":"","content":"Oo! Oo! A Weaver cult could have cyber-fetishes incorporated into cultists, slowly turning them into magitech cyborgs, sleek, deadly and designed to thicken the Gauntlet! They become more and more machine, til the various Weaver-spirits in each fetish-prosthesis merge into one amalgam spirit?<br /> <br /> And a Wyld cult could spend its time gathering and herding Gorgons! Say a neo-pagan believers who refer to Gorgons as \u2018the children of the Eldest Gods\u2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T23:10:46-07:00","id":1494287,"title":"","content":"I would expect many modern Weaver cults to frequently take the form of cybersects. Maybe look into Heaven's Gate some time. They're probably one of the better examples from real life as to what a Weaver cult could look like. I would imagine though that many Weaver cults would not think of themselves as a &quot;cult&quot; because they're not religious. They would take the form of small, science focused groups. During the early part of the last century there were many small eugenics clubs and organizations. Those might be another example of what a Weaver Cult could look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T08:36:40-07:00","id":1494317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494170-wyld-cults-and-weaver-cults?p=1494179#post1494179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld is the kind of being where it doesn't really matter if you worship it or not, the same things still happen. Humans are unlikely to do so in the first place; the books are quite insistent on their lacking a connection it, as if frayed and broken. Still, if a group thinks that they get results from throwing people into a Threshold, they'll probably keep doing it on account of the self same pattern obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Wyld is quite uncaring and quite inconsistant. Unlike the Gods of the Mythos who somehow care nothing about us or the cosmos yet they seem to power and follow the summonings and magics of these irrelevant creatures, the Wyld is truly indifferent. Also being so alien that most people don't even know how to worship it is probably not helpful.<br /> <br /> However, I can see Wyld cults forming around certain Gorgons or Tresholds - for instance someone keeps a twoheaded goat in their basement whose udders produce strange psychodelic substances used and abused in the rites of awakening and transcendance, and the risk if always of not just a bad trip but a poison. Or maybe a creature that commands the faith and following of people who believe it gives them protection but is just a force of nature passing by. There could be people looking for fountains of youth whose consequences and changes may be more psycholgical than physical, or all about exploiting and guarding the strange resources spawning in a living cave that creates impossible materials.<br /> <br /> Weaver cults seem quite simpler in practice. The One Song is broad and all encompassing, and as it's sung people flock to the individuals and places, offering obesiance and faith for order and peace. And with time they turn more and more into drones. These could be tech retreats where new meditation technologies are driven by the strange repetitive white noise, a pristine workshop where youths who came seeking rebellion and electronics come out shiny, chome and obedient or a elderly knitting club encasing the world in weaver's yarn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T09:39:09-07:00","id":1494326,"title":"","content":"....tiny, kind-eyed old women in a knitting circle, using fetish equipment to seal up the local Gauntlet. I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T10:45:24-07:00","id":1494336,"title":"","content":"The idea of a Wyld cult is interesting because I do agree, it seems far more likely that a group of humans with the right resonance (vibes) are more likely to make contact with a particular Wyld-spirit then an avatar of Wyld itself (if such a thing could be said to meaningfully exist outside a pure flow of potentiality). <br /> <br /> I imagine that the kind of group you\u2019d get that would attract/form around a Wyld spirit might resemble practitioners of Chaos Magick or a sort of spiritual nihilism. The embrace of a universe without intrinsic meaning or superstructure, where all things are in truth merely temporary phantasms of the true universe, which is infinite &amp; eternal chaos. <br /> <br /> The issue with that being it would be pretty difficult to imagine such a group or comprehend them, if they were fully enlightened Wyld-cultists. Thankfully for us enlightenment is hard. What you\u2019d probably get instead is a group which espouses those sort of ideas while using a variety of techniques to either detach themselves from the regular mode of reality and experience (psychedelics, shock therapy, physical activity to the point of exhaustion, micro-dosing poison, flatlining, etc.) or embrace that all meaning is a phantasm through devoting themselves to an absurdist principle (parody religions like the Bobbists could be good inspiration for this) or simply devoting themselves to an aspect of the Wyld while recognizing it as a phantasm which only appears distinct from the true chaos of the Wyld due to their lack of perception (this is where you might get cults worshipping specific elemental or the like spirits of the Wyld)<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> Weaver cults on the other hand are interesting I think because they do necessarily admit to an intrinsic meaning and ordering to the world; that there is a place for everything and everything ought to be in its place.<br /> <br /> The big divide which forms then, I imagine, would be between the Dogmatics and the Seekers. The Dogmatics believe that they have knowledge to the proper order of things (or at least a means of accessing it) while the Seekers believe that their IS an order to things, they just don\u2019t know what that order is and are trying to seek it out. While it would be easy to label these seekers as the scientific sort of Weaver-cult (which I think is valid) I think that this sort also has room for more occult and philosophical elements (after all, much of historical occult and philosophical research is dedicated to understanding the order of things in the world).<br /> <br /> Unlike the Wyld however, the Weaver has the presence of mind to take an active role in the affairs of its cults. In cases where a cult has drawn the attention of the Fallen Weaver I do think you get something which resembles what is usually described; a stifling and stagnant order imposed from above by a mad demiurge who can no longer comprehend the necessity of its own limits and which will use the cult to carry out its mad crusade against reality itself and all forms of spiritual resistance; whether Wyld, Wyrm, or Balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T18:14:35-07:00","id":1494370,"title":"","content":"Would psychic Numina be appropriate for a Weaver cult? Like, say, a cyberfetish installed in someone\u2019s brain to \u201cwaken\u201d such abilities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T02:48:22-07:00","id":1494400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494170-wyld-cults-and-weaver-cults?p=1494370#post1494370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would psychic Numina be appropriate for a Weaver cult? Like, say, a cyberfetish installed in someone\u2019s brain to \u201cwaken\u201d such abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your game, man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T19:46:36-07:00","id":1494487,"title":"","content":"I could easily see a Wyld cult being involved with the use of various psychotropic substances (natural, manmade, or paranormal), glossolalia, ritual scarification and other body modification, self-transcendence, mystical trances, out of body experiences, ecstatic religious experiences, and certain Derangements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T13:22:47-07:00","id":1494549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494170-wyld-cults-and-weaver-cults?p=1494487#post1494487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily see a Wyld cult being involved with the use of various psychotropic substances (natural, manmade, or paranormal), glossolalia, ritual scarification and other body modification, self-transcendence, mystical trances, out of body experiences, ecstatic religious experiences, and certain Derangements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld cults probably don't need to make their own drugs. A gorgon probably coughs them up (or acts the part of Exalted's Beasts of Resplendent Liquids). Taste the rainbow!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}